      "level": "warn",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "10 links of appinfo/info.xml lead nowhere:",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/feature-overview.gif]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/main-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/folder-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/tag-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/favorites-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/security-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/search-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/trash-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/settings-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  <screenshot> <![CDATA[https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/marius-wieschollek/passwords/Users/_files/handbook-section.png]]>: not an http(s) URL",
        "  The App Store page shows these links as they are; a reader who follows one ends on an error page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is passwords, the checkout directory is src.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: appinfo/info.xml min-version 8.4; no composer.json in the checkout.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support-max",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml caps PHP at max-version 8.5.",
        "  A server on a newer PHP refuses to enable the app, so this cap has to be raised deliberately with every PHP release, not left where it was."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "No Node version is stated: no engines.node, no .nvmrc, and no node-version in the installed workflows.",
        "  Whoever builds the app uses whatever Node they have, and a build that works on one machine is then not evidence for the next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: none of the configurations this audit looks for.",
        " No ESLint configuration: nothing checks the frontend sources, so a wrong import is found by the build or not at all.",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHPUnit configuration: there is no test harness in the checkout, so nothing can be run against a change.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 32 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 32 to 35; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk)."
      ]
    }
  ],
